course: dictionary
lesson: 1852
title: Seeds that float
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A coconut is the large, hard, hairy brown fruit of a palm tree. Inside it there is white flesh and liquid. The word coconut can also mean just that white flesh, which we use in cooking and sweets. Check which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Scientists study coconuts to learn how seeds travel. «Seeds must travel away from their parent» so that young plants do not have to compete with it for light and water. Some seeds fly, some hook onto fur, and coconuts float.
explain: Context clues help here. «Some seeds float on water, like coconuts» tells you that coconuts float, because the words "like coconuts" show they are an example of seeds that float. Read the words around a new idea before you decide what it means.
fact: A coconut is a noun: one coconut, two coconuts. Coconut meaning the white flesh is uncountable, so you say some coconut, not two coconuts.
fact: «A coconut is a seed in a fibrous, air-filled husk that floats and keeps sea water out.»
fact: A coconut can float for months and travel thousands of kilometres across the sea, and it can still sprout.
fact: «The coconut crab is the largest land crab in the world, it can climb palm trees.»
fact: Coconut milk and coconut water both come from the coconut. Coconut is used in curries, cakes and sweets.
exercise: «Some seeds float on water, like coconuts.» What does this tell you about coconuts? | They are shot out when a pod bursts | *They float on water | They sink straight to the bottom | They can only grow in cold places
exercise: Mum says, «Add some coconut to the curry.» Which meaning of coconut is she using? | A tall tree on a cold mountain | A kind of land crab | *The white flesh used in cooking | The large hairy brown fruit of a palm tree
exercise: «The coconut crab is the largest land crab in the world.» Find and copy one word that means biggest. | crab | *largest | pinch | climb
test: Why can a coconut travel thousands of kilometres across the sea? | It swims with small legs | *Its husk is air-filled, so it floats and keeps sea water out | Birds carry it in their beaks | It is very heavy, so the waves carry it
test: Some games are made so most people lose. Which of these is a coconut shy? | A palm tree on a tropical beach | A crab that can climb palm trees | *A game where balls are thrown at coconuts that are hard to knock down | A cake made with desiccated coconut
exam: «A coconut can float for months and travel thousands of kilometres across the sea and still sprout.» Which clue shows a coconut can travel far? | It is hairy and brown | It has white flesh inside | It is used in curries and cakes | *It can float for months and travel thousands of kilometres
